#edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564458 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186564259 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564458 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186564302 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564458 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564458 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564458 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186564045 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564458 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f1449eb3-c226-5410-a948-814f6bd35c51" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564463 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186564021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564463 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186564227 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564463 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186564239 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564463 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186564244 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564463 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186564278 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564463 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564463 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564463 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186564021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564463 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fbec5fcc-3c3a-5ffd-b0f3-92a5d7992122" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564467 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564467 #edb/ref 1069 "q-158561" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564467 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564467 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the domain of the function $z=\\frac{\\sqrt{y-{x}^{2}}}{2x-y}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564467 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0f0c6fb0-68b0-537c-ab8d-954592bf8ad5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564467 #edb/ref 1074 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y-{x}^{2}\\ge 0 \\\\ 2x-y\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge {x}^{2} \\\\ y\\ne 2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ge {x}^{2},\\,y\\ne 2x\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564477 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564445 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564477 #edb/ref 1069 "q-158199" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564477 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564477 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $g(x,y)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x-y}}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564477 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "28327fac-a614-5756-91bd-3fcab54fcda2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564477 #edb/ref 1074 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the square root is non-negative, and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\nx-y>0\\,⟹\\,y<x\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y<x\\}.\n$$\n\nSince the inequality involves the $>$ sign, the line is not part of the domain. Therefore, we draw a dashed line $y=x$ and shade the area *below* the line.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](images/77/77a1a03d037ee571fb0dc14ec8370c8b01f521b5a54798117c0b131000676599.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564498 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564498 #edb/ref 1069 "q-158186" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564498 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564498 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡y}{{x}^{3}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564498 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7a819c67-d4ea-5946-94af-b50fc8d8ad96" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564498 #edb/ref 1074 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive, and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities: \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y>0 \\\\ {x}^{3}\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}y>0 \\\\ x\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y>0,\\,x\\ne 0\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564504 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564504 #edb/ref 1069 "q-158183" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564504 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564504 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-y)}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564504 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8a09ec73-a8f5-5e32-98fd-165c3e60bda6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564504 #edb/ref 1074 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive, and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities: \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y>0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-y)\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y>0 \\\\ x-y\\ne 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x-y>0,\\,x-y\\ne 1\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564505 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564505 #edb/ref 1069 "q-158549" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564505 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564505 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564505 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8e55ad1f-d84a-5ded-9fca-459293bc995a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564505 #edb/ref 1074 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-1\\ne 0\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}\\ne 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}\\ne 1\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564508 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564387 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564508 #edb/ref 1069 "q-158571" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564508 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564508 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $z=\\frac{2y-x}{{x}^{3}-{y}^{2}-4}$ at the point $(2,-2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564508 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "911398b5-8165-51fb-be3f-bfee0bb6f77f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564508 #edb/ref 1074 "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(2,-2),$ we substitute $x=2$ and $y=-2$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\,{|}_{(2,-2)} & =\\frac{2y-x}{{x}^{3}-{y}^{2}-4}\\,{|}_{(2,-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(-2)-2}{{2}^{3}-(-2)^{2}-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4-2}{8-4-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-6)}{0},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564511 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564511 #edb/ref 1069 "q-158585" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564511 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564511 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $z={2}^{-x}+\\frac{1}{y}$ at the point $(2,2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564511 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9c34765f-7311-53ab-be9b-191b42487450" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564511 #edb/ref 1074 "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(2,2),$ we substitute $x=2$ and $y=2$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\,{|}_{(2,2)} & =({2}^{-x}+\\frac{1}{y}){|}_{(2,2)} \\\\  & ={2}^{-2}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564512 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564443 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564512 #edb/ref 1069 "q-158554" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564512 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564512 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564512 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a1824679-625d-5463-b2f3-fb72a493af82" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564512 #edb/ref 1074 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\ne 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\ne 0\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564517 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564447 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564517 #edb/ref 1069 "q-158194" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564517 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564517 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $g(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4-{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2})?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564517 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "aca8e51f-98b0-5cbe-9d48-2cf6165eb100" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564517 #edb/ref 1074 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n4-{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}>0\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<4\\,⟹\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}<1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}<1\\}.\n$$\n\nSince the expression involves the $<$ sign, the curve is *not* part of the domain. Therefore, we draw the dashed curve $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}<1$ and shade the region *inside* the curve.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](images/59/59ac983361be7dd9a991e1cf134e7193256891a5587eab6bff5edf906fef3688.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
